.TH F_DUPFD_QUERY 2const 2026-10-11 "Linux man-pages (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
F_DUPFD_QUERY
\-
determine whether two file descriptors refer to the same open file description
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ,\~ \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #define _GNU_SOURCE
.B #include <fcntl.h>
.P
.BI "int fcntl(int " fd ", F_DUPFD_QUERY, int " other );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Determine whether file descriptors
.I fd
and
.I other
refer to the same open file description (see
.BR open (2)).
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success,
if both file descriptors refer to the same open file description,
1 is returned;
and if they don't,
0 is returned.
On error,
\-1 is returned,
and
.I errno
is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
See
.BR fcntl (2).
.SH STANDARDS
Linux.
.SH HISTORY
Linux 6.10.
.SH NOTES
This operation is a narrower,
more efficient spelling of the following
.BR kcmp (2)
invocation:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
pid_t  pid;
\&
pid = getpid();
if (syscall(SYS_kcmp, pid, pid, KCMP_FILE, fd, other) == 0) {
	/* fd and other refer to the same open file description */
}
.EE
.in
.SH EXAMPLES
The following program checks
whether the standard output and standard error streams
refer to the same open file description
(typically, the user's terminal).
Example output:
.P
.in +4n
.EX
.RB $ " ./a.out"
stdout and stderr refer to the same open file description
.RB $ " ./a.out 2>/dev/null"
stdout and stderr refer to different open file descriptions
.RB $ " ./a.out >/dev/tty 2>/dev/null"
stdout and stderr refer to different open file descriptions
.EE
.in
.SS Program source
.\" SRC BEGIN (dupfd_query.c)
.EX
#define _GNU_SOURCE
#include <err.h>
#include <fcntl.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <unistd.h>
\&
int
main(void)
{
	int  ret;
\&
	ret = fcntl(STDOUT_FILENO, F_DUPFD_QUERY, STDERR_FILENO);
	if (ret == \-1)
		err(EXIT_FAILURE, "fcntl");
\&
	printf("stdout and stderr refer to %s\[rs]n",
	       ret ? "the same file open file description"
	           : "different open file descriptions");
}
.EE
.\" SRC END
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dup (2),
.BR fcntl (2),
.BR kcmp (2),
.BR open (2)
